Hi John,

It really helps if you provide your data in a way that we can easily
use - it saves a lot of time mucking around to get the data into R.  I
also suspect that you want 100's in the data frame and not 1's, and
the new row makes more sense at the top of the existing data.   I've
given one approach to solve your problem with the plyr package
(http://had.co.nz/plyr).

